.TH HD-HARDEN 8 "November 2026" "hd-base" "HyprDebian"
.SH NAME
hd-harden \- harden the SSH server, the kernel, the home directories and the firewall
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B hd-harden
.RB [ \-\-ssh ]
.RB [ \-\-sysctl ]
.RB [ \-\-modules ]
.RB [ \-\-zfs ]
.RB [ \-\-ufw ]
.RB [ \-\-all ]
.RB [ \-\-json ]
.RB [ \-\-network
.IR cidr ]...
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B hd-harden
hardens the parts of the system that its options name; they can be combined.
Running it again changes nothing.
Run it as root.
.PP
Without options it shows for each part whether it is hardened:
.B on
or
.BR off ,
or
.B changed
when the file it writes has other content, as after an edit by hand or
from an older
.BR hd-harden .
The state of ufw shows only for root, who can read its rules; for other
users it is
.BR unknown .
With
.B \-\-json
it prints the same as a JSON object, with the state of each part, which
.BR hd-report (8)
sends to the dashboard:
.PP
.RS
.nf
{"ssh": "on", "sysctl": "on", "modules": "changed", "zfs": "off", "ufw": "on"}
.fi
.RE
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-ssh
Turns off password logins, root logins and X11 forwarding of the SSH
server, with
.BR "PasswordAuthentication no" ,
.BR "KbdInteractiveAuthentication no" ,
.B PermitRootLogin no
and
.B X11Forwarding no
in
.IR /etc/ssh/sshd_config.d/10\-hd\-harden.conf .
.BR sshd (8)
takes the first value it reads, and the file comes before
.I sshd_config
and the later files of
.IR sshd_config.d .
It stops before writing when no user of the group
.BR sudo ,
as a member or by their own group, has an
.I ~/.ssh/authorized_keys
that is not empty, as nobody could get root over ssh then.
It checks the config with
.BR "sshd \-t" ,
puts the old file back when that fails, and reloads the SSH server.
.TP
.B \-\-sysctl
Writes
.I /etc/sysctl.d/90\-hd\-harden.conf
and loads it:
.B kernel.yama.ptrace_scope
1, so a process can only ptrace its children,
.B kernel.kptr_restrict
1, which hides the kernel addresses in
.I /proc
from users without
.BR CAP_SYSLOG ,
and
.B dev.tty.ldisc_autoload
0, so only root can load the module of a line discipline.
.TP
.B \-\-modules
Writes
.I /etc/modprobe.d/hd\-harden.conf
with
.B install
.I module
.B /bin/false
for each module that is never loaded, also not with
.BR modprobe (8):
the network protocols
.BR dccp ,
.BR sctp ,
.B rds
and
.BR tipc ,
which the kernel loads when any user opens a socket of them, the line
discipline
.BR n_hdlc ,
which any user can attach to a tty, and the rarely used file systems
.BR cramfs ,
.BR freevxfs ,
.B jffs2
and
.BR hfs .
.B hfsplus
and
.B udf
stay, for disks of macOS and for DVDs.
A module that is loaded already stays loaded until a reboot;
.B hd-harden
names it.
.TP
.B \-\-zfs
Sets
.B setuid=off
and
.B devices=off
on the ZFS dataset mounted at
.IR /home ,
so no program below
.I /home
runs with the rights of its owner and no device file there opens a device.
The datasets of the users below it inherit that.
ZFS mounts only the dataset it set them on again with
.B nosuid
and
.BR nodev ,
so
.B hd-harden
mounts again those below it that are mounted without them.
The state of
.B \-\-zfs
is
.B off
as long as one of them is mounted without them, and names it.
.B exec
stays on, for
.IR ~/.local/bin .
.TP
.B \-\-ufw
Lets ssh in from the local IPv4 networks alone.
It adds a rule
.B allow from
.I network
.B to any port 22 proto tcp
to
.BR ufw (8)
for each IPv4 network of the global addresses of the interfaces that
systemd-networkd configures, as
.B networkctl list
shows them, or for each network given with
.BR \-\-network .
Then it deletes the rules of
.B ufw show added
that let ssh in from anywhere, by the name
.BR SSH ,
.BR OpenSSH ,
.B 22
or
.BR 22/tcp ,
such as the
.B ufw allow SSH
of the installer.
That covers IPv4 and IPv6, so ssh no longer comes in over IPv6.
The bridges of Docker are not configured by systemd-networkd, so their
networks get no rule, and the route rules of ufw, which open the ports of the
containers of
.BR hd-docker (7),
stay as they are.
The new rules come first, so a connection from a local network is never
refused, and connections that are open stay open, as ufw lets established
connections through.
.TP
.B \-\-all
All of
.BR \-\-ssh ,
.BR \-\-sysctl ,
.BR \-\-modules ,
.B \-\-zfs
and
.BR \-\-ufw .
.TP
.B \-\-json
Show what is hardened as a JSON object, without the options that harden.
.TP
.BR \-\-network " " \fIcidr\fR
With
.B \-\-ufw
or
.BR \-\-all ,
an IPv4 network to let ssh in from, such as
.BR 192.168.1.0/24 ,
in place of those of the interfaces.
It may be given more than once.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show a short help and exit.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 when everything was hardened or the state was shown, 1 when a step
failed, and 2 for wrong arguments.
The steps before the one that failed stay done.
.SH EXAMPLES
Show what is hardened:
.PP
.RS
.nf
sudo hd-harden
.fi
.RE
.PP
Harden all of it:
.PP
.RS
.nf
sudo hd-harden \-\-all
.fi
.RE
.PP
Let ssh in from one network alone:
.PP
.RS
.nf
sudo hd-harden \-\-ufw \-\-network 192.168.1.0/24
.fi
.RE
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/ssh/sshd_config.d/10\-hd\-harden.conf
The hardening of the SSH server, written by
.BR \-\-ssh .
.TP
.I /etc/sysctl.d/90\-hd\-harden.conf
The hardening sysctls, written by
.BR \-\-sysctl .
.TP
.I /etc/modprobe.d/hd\-harden.conf
The modules that are never loaded, written by
.BR \-\-modules .
.TP
.I /usr/share/hd-base/templates/hd\-harden\-sshd.conf.j2
.TQ
.I /usr/share/hd-base/templates/hd\-harden\-sysctl.conf.j2
.TQ
.I /usr/share/hd-base/templates/hd\-harden\-modprobe.conf.j2
The templates of those files.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR hd-base (7),
.BR hd-report (8),
.BR hd-docker (7),
.BR sshd_config (5),
.BR sysctl.d (5),
.BR modprobe.d (5),
.BR zfsprops (7),
.BR ufw (8),
.BR networkctl (1)
